<title>BELGIUM: ANTWERP PORT WINS PULP TRAFFIC FROM ROTTERDAM.</title>
<headline>ANTWERP PORT WINS PULP TRAFFIC FROM ROTTERDAM.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port of Antwerp said in a statement that Noorse Star Shipping had switched landing its U.S. pulp cargo to Antwerp from Rotterdam.</p>
<p>The move represents a gain of around 230,000 tonnes of wood products traffic a year, the Port said.</p>
<p>&quot;The move was not motivated by any discontent with Rotterdam,&quot; the Belgian port, Europe's second largest after its Dutch neighbour, said. Star had switched to Antwerp because of the possibilities the port offered for filling up its ships with steel, containers and other goods for the return voyage to the U.S..</p>
